{"id":"2a91ae6809cec03c","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-dual-pairing.md","title":"Dual Pairing","display":"df-dual-pairing — Dual Pairing","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-dual-pairing","aliases":["58-df-dual-pairing"],"display":"df-dual-pairing — Dual Pairing","depends_on":["[[58-df-vector-space]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-dual-pairing"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-dual-pairing</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-dual-pairing — Dual Pairing"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y\">\\(X,Y\\)</span> (complex vector-space carriers with operations <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_X,\\cdot_X\">\\(+_X,\\cdot_X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_Y,\\cdot_Y\">\\(+_Y,\\cdot_Y\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B:X\\times Y\\to\\mathbb C\">\\(B:X\\times Y\\to\\mathbb C\\)</span> (pairing candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S\\)</span> (fully explicit vector-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"592f9cfb66a507c2\" href=\"?note=592f9cfb66a507c2\" title=\"58-df-vector-space\">58-df-vector-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B)\">\\(\\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B)\\)</span> (dual-pairing predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(X,\\mathbb C,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(Y,\\mathbb C,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(B,X\\times Y,\\mathbb C)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle a\\cdot_Xx_1+_Xb\\cdot_Xx_2,y\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle x,a\\cdot_Yy_1+_Yb\\cdot_Yy_2\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)\\land\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall x\\in X\\;(B(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)=B(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle))\\right]\\to y_1=y_2\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(X,\\mathbb C,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(Y,\\mathbb C,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(B,X\\times Y,\\mathbb C)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle a\\cdot_Xx_1+_Xb\\cdot_Xx_2,y\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle x,a\\cdot_Yy_1+_Yb\\cdot_Yy_2\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)\\land\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall x\\in X\\;(B(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)=B(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle))\\right]\\to y_1=y_2\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing\\text{-}separates\\text{-}left} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\to\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing\\text{-}separates\\text{-}left} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\to\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(X, Y)\">\\((X, Y)\\)</span> is a dual pair if the bilinear form is separating.</li>\n<li>Both vector-space operation pairs occur in the predicate signature; changing either structure on the same carriers can change whether <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B\">\\(B\\)</span> is bilinear.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma(X, Y)\">\\(\\sigma(X, Y)\\)</span>-topology on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> is generated by seminorms <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p_y(x) = |\\langle x, y \\rangle|\">\\(p_y(x) = |\\langle x, y \\rangle|\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The Mackey topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau(X,Y)\">\\(\\tau(X,Y)\\)</span> is the topology of uniform convergence on absolutely convex <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma(Y,X)\">\\(\\sigma(Y,X)\\)</span>-compact subsets of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Y\">\\(Y\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The pairing embeds <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Y\">\\(Y\\)</span> into the algebraic dual of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> into the algebraic dual of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Y\">\\(Y\\)</span>; it need not identify either space with the whole dual.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-vector-space","status":"resolved","id":"592f9cfb66a507c2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-vector-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-vector-space","status":"resolved","id":"592f9cfb66a507c2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S$ (fully explicit vector-space predicate, see [[58-df-vector-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (set-function predicate, see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,Y","display":false},{"tex":"+_X,\\cdot_X","display":false},{"tex":"+_Y,\\cdot_Y","display":false},{"tex":"B:X\\times Y\\to\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(X,\\mathbb C,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{VectorSpace}_S(Y,\\mathbb C,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0,1)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(B,X\\times Y,\\mathbb C)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle a\\cdot_Xx_1+_Xb\\cdot_Xx_2,y\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall a,b\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(B(\\langle x,a\\cdot_Yy_1+_Yb\\cdot_Yy_2\\rangle)=aB(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)+bB(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle)\\right)\\land\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)\\land\\forall y_1,y_2\\in Y\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall x\\in X\\;(B(\\langle x,y_1\\rangle)=B(\\langle x,y_2\\rangle))\\right]\\to y_1=y_2\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dual\\text{-}pairing\\text{-}separates\\text{-}left} \\vdash \\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)\\to\\forall x_1,x_2\\in X\\;\\left(\\left[\\forall y\\in Y\\;(B(\\langle x_1,y\\rangle)=B(\\langle x_2,y\\rangle))\\right]\\to x_1=x_2\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"(X, Y)","display":false},{"tex":"B","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma(X, Y)","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"p_y(x) = |\\langle x, y \\rangle|","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau(X,Y)","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma(Y,X)","display":false},{"tex":"Y","display":false},{"tex":"Y","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"Y","display":false}],"bytes":2540,"backlinks":[{"id":"b1484ba48c364679","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$B:X\\times Y\\to\\mathbb C$ and $\\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}(X,Y,B,+_X,\\cdot_X,+_Y,\\cdot_Y)$ is the fully explicit dual-pairing predicate from [[58-df-dual-pairing]]."},{"id":"c0fe5ecedfe72c4b","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{DualPairing}_{\\mathbb C}$ is the predicate from [[58-df-dual-pairing]]."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-457","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-dual-pairing.md|58-df-dual-pairing]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["592f9cfb66a507c2","36d7463d215be751"]}